# React & Next.js Patterns — VTC Apps

Auth bootstrap: `auth-bootstrap.mdc`. Prefer **API routes** over Server Actions for authenticated data (JWT in query param).

## Rules of Hooks

ALL hooks at top, before conditional returns.

```typescript
export default function MyPage() {
  const hasAccess = useAdminAccess()
  const [data, setData] = useState(null)
  useEffect(() => { /* ... */ }, [])
  if (hasAccess === null) return <LoadingSpinner />
  if (hasAccess === false) return null
  return <div>{/* JSX */}</div>
}
```

## Auth on mount

```typescript
const [mounted, setMounted] = useState(false)
useEffect(() => {
  setMounted(true)
  bootstrapAuthFromUrl()
}, [])
if (!mounted) return <LoadingSpinner />
```

## Re-render Loops

Do not put `searchParams` / `router` in `useEffect` deps when navigating. Use ref guard + `window.location.href` for one-time redirects.

## Hydration

All `localStorage` / `window` access after `mounted` is true.

## useEffect

- Cleanup subscriptions/timers
- `hasFetchedRef` to avoid double-fetch in strict mode

## State

Never mutate arrays/objects in place — spread/map/filter.

## Next.js

- Wrap `useSearchParams()` in `<Suspense>` at layout
- `'use client'` for hooks and browser APIs
- Dynamic params in Next.js 15+: `const { id } = await params`
- **Avoid Server Actions for auth** unless token is explicitly passed; standard path is `fetch(addTokenToUrl('/api/...'))`

## useAdminAccess (convention)

Hook returns `null` (loading), `false` (denied), `true` (allowed). Fetch role from an API route using `addTokenToUrl`, or derive from client-known `posif_group` after bootstrap.
